From 4cd02189eba0473722907293730c5176cbdcef84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roland Nagtegaal <perpetualbits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:25:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vkgears: guard the optional wl_seat on teardown

fini_display() calls wl_seat_destroy(keyboard_data.seat) unconditionally,
but a wl_seat is optional: registry_handle_global() only assigns the seat
when the compositor advertises one. A compositor with no input devices --
headless weston, for instance -- advertises none, keyboard_data.seat stays
NULL, and the demo segfaults on exit.

The keyboard immediately above it is already guarded the same way; only
the seat was missed.

Reproduced with vkgears against a seatless compositor: stock exits 139
(SIGSEGV), guarded exits cleanly at 60.062 FPS, same compositor, back to
back.
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wayland.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wayland.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wayland.c
index 56ef2b3..185daec 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wayland.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wayland.c
@@ -277,7 +277,11 @@ fini_display()
 
    libdecor_unref(decor_context);
 
-   wl_seat_destroy(keyboard_data.seat);
+   /* A wl_seat is optional: a compositor with no input devices advertises
+    * none, leaving keyboard_data.seat NULL, and wl_seat_destroy() would
+    * dereference it. */
+   if (keyboard_data.seat)
+      wl_seat_destroy(keyboard_data.seat);
    xkb_context_unref(keyboard_data.xkb_context);
    wl_compositor_destroy(compositor);
    wl_display_flush(display);
-- 
